## 4. Experimental Section
Synthesis of ZIF-8 via Mechanochemical Synthesis: Typically, 40.5 mg nano ZnO (0.5 mmol) and 82.1 mg 2-methylimidazole (1 mmol) were first mixed in 25 mL cylindrical zirconia jars (external diameter: 49 mm; inner diameter: 32 mm; height: 55 mm) with zirconia balls (ball diameter: 3 mm × 70, ball diameter: 5 mm × 30, and ball diameter: 8 mm × 5), followed by the addition of 60 μL ethanol. The precursors were next ground at 480 rpm for 5 min on an XQM-0.4A ball mill from CHANGSHA TIANCHUANG POWDER TECHNOLOGY CO., LTD. The ZIF-8 powder was centrifuged, washed with ethanol three times, and vacuum dried at room temperature. Synthesis of \(\mathrm{Ag}_{44}@\mathrm{ZIF}-8\): The ZIF-8 seed was first synthesized by grinding nano ZnO (0.25 mmol) and 2-methylimidazole (0.5 mmol) in the presence of EtOH (60 μL) for 3 min at 480 rpm. Then, DMF solutions of \(\mathrm{Ag}_{44}(p\mathrm{-}\mathrm{MBA})_{30}^{4-}\) (100 μL) and residual starting material (ZnO, 0.25 mmol; 2-methylimidazole, 0.5 mmol) were added and ground for a further 2 min. The assisting solvents were volatile and would deplete in the first step. The product was recovered and additionally washed with DMF to remove \(\mathrm{Ag}_{44}\) that surface adsorbed on the frameworks, followed by the conventional wash step. Finally, nanocomposites should be carefully dried since the loss of the coordinate solvent on the nanocluster might destroy APNCs.
Synthesis of \(\mathrm{Au}_{25}@\mathrm{HOF}-101\): As a typical run, 1,3,6,8-tetrakis (benzoic acid) pyrene (0.075 mmol) was placed in zirconia jars with 3 g zirconia ball, followed by the addition of 60 μL EtOH. The precursors were then ground at 480 rpm for 10 min. Then, \(\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}\) solutions of \(\mathrm{Au}_{25}\) (L-Cys)18 (100 μL) and residual 1,3,6,8-tetrakis (benzoic acid) pyrene (0.075 mmol) were added and ground for a further 5 min. The product was recovered and washed with \(\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}\) to remove \(\mathrm{Au}_{25}\) that surface adsorbed on HOF-101, then dried under vacuum at room temperature.
Synthesis of Other APNCs@Frameworks: The nanocomposites were synthesized in two steps to avoid the influence of the assisting solvent (such as EtOH and DMSO) on APNC structures. The crystal seeds of frameworks were first constructed with half the precursors in the presence of the assisting solvent. APNCs and the residual precursors were introduced in the next step without the assisting solvent. It should be noticed that the APNCs were first dissolved in their corresponding solvent before introduction to make them disperse homogeneously, such as DMF for \((\mathrm{Ag}_{44}(p\mathrm{-}\mathrm{MBA})_{30})^{4-}\); \(\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}\) for \(\mathrm{Au}_{25}\) (L-Cys)18 and water-soluble APNCs; DCM for \((\mathrm{Pd}_{3}\mathrm{Cl}(\mathrm{PPh}_{2})_{2}(\mathrm{PPh}_{3})_{3})^{+}\)and oil-soluble APNCs. The amount of the introduced APNCs could be tuned by changing the concentration of the APNC solution.
Synthesis of \(\mathrm{GOx}/\mathrm{Au}_{25}@\mathrm{UiO}-66\): The Zr cluster (acted as the \(\mathrm{Zr}_{6}\) metal node in UiO-66) was first synthesized. Methacrylic acid (2.8 mL) was first injected into 4 mL \(\mathrm{Zr}(\mathrm{OP})_{4}\) solution (70% solution in \(n\)-propanol), and 60 μL water was next added to the solution. The above mixture was placed in an oven at 60 °C for three days. Then, the colorless Zr cluster was filtered and washed with \(n\)-propanol.
material (Zr cluster, \(0.015\,\mathsf{mmol}\); and terephthalic acid, \(0.09\,\mathsf{mmol}\)), \(20\,\mathsf{mg}\) glucose oxidase \((\mathsf{G O x})\), and \(50\,\upmu\mathrm{L}\,\mathsf{A u}_{25}(\mathsf{L-C y s})_{18}\) \((0.1\,\mathsf{mg})\) were added and ground for a further 5 min. The \(\mathsf{G O x}/\mathsf{A u}_{25}\ @\mathsf{U i O-66}\) powder was recovered and washed with water 3 times and then freeze-dried.
General Procedure for the HRP-Mimicking Reaction: In a typical run, \(3,3^{\prime},5,5^{\prime}\)-tetramethylbenzidine solution (TMB, \(5\,\mathsf{mM}\)) was first prepared using DMSO as the solvent, the free \(\mathsf{A u}_{25}\) solution and immobilized \(\mathsf{A u}_{25}\ @\mathsf{U i O-66}\) suspensions were adjusted to give similar Au concentration at \(0.1\,\mathsf{mg\,mL}^{-1}\) in \(50\,\mathsf{mM}\) acetate buffer solution \((\mathsf{pH}\,4.0)\). The \(\mathsf{A u}_{25}\ @\mathsf{H O F-101}\) suspensions were adjusted to provide a much lower Au concentration at \(0.001\,\mathsf{mg\,mL}^{-1}\) in \(50\,\mathsf{mM}\) acetate buffer solution \((\mathsf{pH}\,4.0)\). The reactions were carried out at \(30\,^{\circ}\mathsf{C}\) in a cuvette containing \(600\,\upmu\mathrm{L}\) acetate buffer \((\mathsf{pH}\,4.0)\), \(100\,\upmu\mathrm{L}\) of \(5\,\mathsf{mM}\) TMR, and \(50\,\upmu\mathrm{L}\) cluster solution/suspensions \((5\,\upmu\mathrm{g}\) based on Au for free \(\mathsf{A u}_{25}\) and \(\mathsf{A u}_{25}\ @\mathsf{U i O-66}\), \(0.05\,\upmu\mathrm{g}\) based on Au for \(\mathsf{A u}_{25}\ @\mathsf{H O F-101}\)), and the reaction was initiated by adding \(200\,\upmu\mathrm{L}\) of \(100\,\mathsf{mM}\,\mathsf{H}_{2}\mathsf{O}_{2}\). The absorbance of the solution was measured at \(652\,\mathsf{nm}\) after being stirred various times. For free horseradish peroxidase (HRP), the catalytic procedure was similar to the HRP-mimicking reaction, except using HRP as the catalyst instead of \(\mathsf{A u}_{25}\). All reactions were repeated at least four times.
General Operation of Enzyme-Clusterzyme Cascade Reaction: In a typical run, \(o\)-phenylenediamine solution (OPD, \(10\,\mathsf{mM}\)) was first prepared using acetate buffer solution \((\mathsf{pH}\,4.0)\) as the solvent. The reactions were carried out at \(35\,^{\circ}\mathsf{C}\) in a cuvette containing \(950\,\upmu\mathrm{L}\) OPD solution \((10\,\mathsf{mM}\), \(\mathsf{pH}\,4.0)\) and \(\mathsf{G O x}/\mathsf{A u}_{25}\ @\mathsf{U i O-66}\) (containing \(0.5\,\mathsf{mg\,G O}\) and \(10\,\upmu\mathrm{g}\,\mathsf{A u}_{25}\)). The reaction was initiated by adding \(50\,\upmu\mathrm{L}\) of \(500\,\mathsf{mM}\) glucose solution, followed by incubation at room temperature for the desired time. The oxidation of OPD was detected by UV–vis spectroscopy at a wavelength of \(420\,\mathsf{nm}\). In control experiments, the same amount of free enzyme/clusterzyme (the concentrations of \(\mathsf{G O x}\) and \(\mathsf{A u}_{25}\) were \(0.5\,\mathsf{mg\,mL}^{-1}\) and \(10\,\upmu\mathrm{g\,mL}^{-1}\), respectively) were used to drive the cascade reaction.
